al removal for ordered binary matrices","statements":["MatrixRemoval"]}],"scope":"The formalized result disproves a polynomial removal bound for one explicit $66\\times66$ binary pattern. For every $c,C>0$, there is an $n\\times n$ binary matrix at normalized edit distance at least $\\varepsilon>0$ from being pattern-free but with fewer than $c\\varepsilon^C n^{132}$ induced ordered copies. Row and column indices are independently increasing, and every zero and one entry must match. The construction gives an explicit sequence of such matrices, allowing edits in both directions.","title":"Polynomial removal fails for ordered binary matrices","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/190.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":null,"reading":"reading:15f23d8d038396d98b933927","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":"`no_polynomial_removal_bound : ∀ c C > 0, ∃ n ≥ 1, ∃ ε ∈ (0,1), ∃ A : BinaryMatrix n, fixedDistance A ≥ ε ∧ copyCount fixedH A < c * ε^C * n^132` for the explicit 66x66 `fixedH`; `copyCount` counts pairs of strictly increasing row/column maps with `A (r i) (c j) = H i j` (ordered, zeros and ones matched) and `fixedMinEdits` is a true min Hamming distance to pattern-free matrices (junk branch n*n+1 exceeds any distance). Matches the summary and docs.","reading":"reading:e7525260605ca623b027a49f","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:15f23d8d038396d98b933927","reading:e7525260605ca623b027a49f"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin