,"kind":"pairing-review","reason":"Recorded candidate or producer-declared correspondences have no pair-specific review.","target":"f:190"}],"schema":"statement-map-web/2","selection":{"headline_state":"candidate","headline_statement":"r:Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026:thm:main","lean":"l:MatrixRemoval","method":"Show catalogue candidate separately; use unambiguous manifest bindings or source-cited targets, abstain on unresolved citations, then use lexical candidates. Prefer a producer main-result Lean object with an available target.","paired_statement":"r:Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026:thm:main","pairing_state":"candidate-pairing","scope_context":"family-readings"},"source_associations":[],"statements":[{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:437d0f336a75a58c38bf76654e52f187c8705eaf2ba8991ce33433616e67badb","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026#thm:main","title":"thm:main"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/e557ad24cf402673ef70333b.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","id":"r:Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026:thm:main","manuscript_id":"p:Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026","name":"thm:main","printed_number":"1.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"8056826bbd00caea871ad036bd295182e2bef3e2","binding":{"file":"build/sections/01-introduction.tex","label":"thm:main","line":33,"manuscript":"Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026","statement_sha256":"779170032e8cc4f85c77ce4830a5fbc2c15fc6de25fa1775d27d90718443eee8"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"8056826bbd00caea871ad036bd295182e2bef3e2","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026.html#thm:main","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a5e37e3203800363495306a25f7cd52a3a91d46e779be9bad72257ce5b1a18f0","file":"preprints/Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":33,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"779170032e8cc4f85c77ce4830a5fbc2c15fc6de25fa1775d27d90718443eee8","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a5e37e3203800363495306a25f7cd52a3a91d46e779be9bad72257ce5b1a18f0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Polynomial-removal-fails-for-ordered-binary-matrices-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L33"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a fixed binary $66\\times66$ matrix $H$ with the following\nproperty. For every integer $h\\ge1$, put\n\\[\n n_h=(386h+2)2^h,\\qquad \\epsilon_h=(386h+2)^{-2}.\n\\]\nThere is a binary $n_h\\times n_h$ matrix $A_h$ such that\n\\[\n \\operatorname{dist}_H(A_h)\\ge\\epsilon_h,\n \\qquad\n \\frac{N_H(A_h)}{n_h^{132}}\\le\\epsilon_h2^{-h}.\n\\]\nConsequently, no positive constants $c,C$ give a polynomial removal\nbound for this fixed $H$."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerpr